WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:37.778
Oxford Bookworms Stage 1 The Omega Files Short Stories by Jennifer Bassett Read by Gareth Armstrong Published and copyright, Oxford University Press 2007 EDI, European Department of Intelligence.

00:00:37.838 --> 00:00:43.700
There were two of them, Hawker and Jude.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:50.362
They had no other names, just Hawker and Jude.

00:00:50.422 --> 00:00:55.454
They were young, fast and clever.

00:00:55.514 --> 00:01:02.026
They worked for EDI in the European government.

00:01:02.086 --> 00:01:09.470
You know about the Americans CIA and the Russians KGB?

00:01:09.530 --> 00:01:26.791
Well, this was EDI, the European Department of Intelligence, big secrets, very strange secrets, the secrets of the Omega files.

00:01:26.850 --> 00:01:33.904
They don't get into the newspapers and most people never hear about them.

00:01:33.964 --> 00:01:40.658
Most people don't know anything about EDI.

00:01:40.718 --> 00:01:46.741
In the early years, Hawker and Jude traveled a lot.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:02:03.850
Brussels, Strasbourg, Rome, Delhi, Washington, North Africa, South America, Australia, no home no family, just work.

00:02:03.910 --> 00:02:12.676
They worked for the top man in the Brussels office of EDI, and only for him.

00:02:12.736 --> 00:02:16.020
He was called Arla.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:21.094
Nobody knew his real name, or much about him.

00:02:21.154 --> 00:02:24.336
Some said he was Latvian.

00:02:24.396 --> 00:02:29.016
Others said he was from another planet.

00:02:29.076 --> 00:02:43.688
He always gave the hard jobs to Hawker and Jude, the jobs with questions but not many answers, the Omega files.

00:02:43.748 --> 00:02:52.332
When I met them many years later, Hawker and Jude were about 70 years old.

00:02:52.392 --> 00:02:59.209
They lived very quietly in a little white house on a Greek island.

00:02:59.269 --> 00:03:03.954
They went walking, swimming, fishing.

00:03:04.014 --> 00:03:08.755
They sat in the sun and slept a lot.

00:03:08.815 --> 00:03:14.916
At first, they didn't want to talk about their work.

00:03:14.976 --> 00:03:18.307
We can't, said Jude.

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:20.738
Our work was secret.

00:03:20.798 --> 00:03:26.970
It's all in the government files and nobody can read them.

00:03:27.029 --> 00:03:33.944
After 30 years, I said, People can read all secret government files.

00:03:34.004 --> 00:03:37.857
Not these files, Hawker said.

00:03:37.917 --> 00:03:44.490
It's a hundred years before people can read the EDI files.

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.762
I looked at them.

00:03:46.822 --> 00:03:51.304
But I don't need to read the files, I said.

00:03:51.364 --> 00:03:55.326
I can get the stories from you.

00:03:55.386 --> 00:03:57.698
And I did.

00:03:57.758 --> 00:04:08.564
Here are some of them.

00:04:08.624 --> 00:04:24.227
Omega File 349 London, England.

00:04:24.287 --> 00:04:33.044
There's a young man in London called Johnny Cook, said.

00:04:33.104 --> 00:04:36.798
He's about 18.

00:04:36.857 --> 00:04:44.324
He doesn't have a home But he goes clubbing nearly every night.

00:04:44.384 --> 00:04:50.489
Those all night dance clubs for young people.

00:04:50.549 --> 00:04:55.212
Here's a photograph of him.

00:04:55.272 --> 00:05:03.378
He put the photograph on the table, and Jude and Hawker looked at it.

00:05:03.438 --> 00:05:13.741
And, Hawker said, he wants to sell a story to a newspaper, Arla said.

00:05:13.801 --> 00:05:18.723
Some story about a drug company.

00:05:18.783 --> 00:05:20.674
Find him.

00:05:20.734 --> 00:05:22.704
Talk to him.

00:05:22.764 --> 00:05:25.445
What's his story?

00:05:25.505 --> 00:05:28.516
I want to know.

00:05:28.576 --> 00:05:37.946
Jude and Hawker took an afternoon plane from Brussels to London, and then went to a hotel.

00:05:37.966 --> 00:05:44.439
"'What are you going to wear tonight?'

00:05:44.499 --> 00:05:46.270
said Jude.

00:05:46.330 --> 00:05:49.572
"'Not those old jeans, please.

00:05:49.592 --> 00:05:52.574
"'What's wrong with them?'

00:05:52.633 --> 00:05:53.614
Hawker said.

00:05:53.634 --> 00:05:56.086
"'We're going clubbing.

00:05:56.145 --> 00:05:59.472
Not out to dinner at the Ritz Hotel.

00:05:59.532 --> 00:06:04.159
Well, wear a different shirt, then.

00:06:04.219 --> 00:06:06.610
That one's dirty.

00:06:06.670 --> 00:06:10.532
You can wash it for me," Hawker said.

00:06:10.592 --> 00:06:14.004
Get lost, said Jude.

00:06:14.064 --> 00:06:21.828
They had dinner, watched television for an hour or two, and then went out.

00:06:21.888 --> 00:06:27.351
It was a warm night with a little rain now and then.

00:06:27.411 --> 00:06:31.674
London weather said Hawker.

00:06:31.734 --> 00:06:36.987
They found a taxi with a young driver and got in.

00:06:37.007 --> 00:06:40.629
"'We're two,' said the driver.

00:06:40.649 --> 00:06:44.811
"'We want to go clubbing,' Jude said.

00:06:44.831 --> 00:06:48.173
"'Where's the best place this week?

00:06:48.193 --> 00:06:49.894
"'Do you know?

00:06:49.914 --> 00:06:53.676
"'Bru knows,' the driver said.

00:06:53.696 --> 00:06:58.640
"'Or Garcia's down by the river.

00:06:58.700 --> 00:07:01.834
Everybody's going there this week."

00:07:01.894 --> 00:07:03.386
Okay.

00:07:03.446 --> 00:07:06.658
Let's go, said Hawker.

00:07:06.718 --> 00:07:12.922
They went to Garcia's first, then moved on to Bruno's.

00:07:12.982 --> 00:07:19.378
They found Johnny Cook in a third club called Monty's.

00:07:19.438 --> 00:07:22.620
It was two o'clock in the morning.

00:07:22.680 --> 00:07:26.352
That's him all right, Hawker said.

00:07:26.412 --> 00:07:28.556
Look at his ear.

00:07:28.616 --> 00:07:39.374
Johnny Cook was tall and thin, with long yellow hair and two black earrings in his left ear.

00:07:39.434 --> 00:07:41.596
Johnny!

00:07:41.656 --> 00:07:43.618
Johnny Cook!

00:07:43.678 --> 00:07:46.288
shouted Jude suddenly.

00:07:46.348 --> 00:07:51.482
She ran and put her arms round Johnny Cook's neck.

00:07:51.542 --> 00:07:53.874
Hi, Johnny!

00:07:53.934 --> 00:07:55.775
You remember me?

00:07:55.835 --> 00:07:57.166
Jude!

00:07:57.226 --> 00:07:59.051
We met last week.

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:00.776
at Garcia's.

00:08:00.836 --> 00:08:02.708
You remember?

00:08:02.768 --> 00:08:06.420
Oh, this is my friend, Hawker.

00:08:06.480 --> 00:08:07.992
Hi, Johnny.

00:08:08.052 --> 00:08:11.034
Good to meet you, said Hawker.

00:08:11.094 --> 00:08:14.417
Hi, said Johnny Cook.

00:08:14.476 --> 00:08:16.598
He looked at Jude.

00:08:16.658 --> 00:08:19.610
Did we meet at Garcia's?

00:08:19.670 --> 00:08:23.604
Of course we did, laughed Jude.

00:08:23.664 --> 00:08:27.807
I was with Sara and Patty and the others.

00:08:27.867 --> 00:08:29.420
Remember?

00:08:29.480 --> 00:08:33.666
Oh, yeah, said Johnny.

00:08:33.686 --> 00:08:34.806
I remember.

00:08:34.866 --> 00:08:36.528
He looked around.

00:08:36.589 --> 00:08:40.091
Are they here tonight?

00:08:40.111 --> 00:08:44.394
No, it's just me and Hawker tonight, said Jude.

00:08:44.454 --> 00:08:48.017
Come on, let's dance.

00:08:48.077 --> 00:08:51.130
They danced for two hours.

00:08:51.190 --> 00:08:58.336
Then they left with about ten other people and went across the river to a new club.

00:08:58.396 --> 00:09:04.882
The music there was louder and the dancing was very fast.

00:09:04.942 --> 00:09:12.508
After two more hours of dancing, Hawker was hot, tired and thirsty.

00:09:12.568 --> 00:09:16.221
I'm getting old, he said to Jude.

00:09:16.281 --> 00:09:19.493
Don't these people ever go to bed?

00:09:19.554 --> 00:09:23.116
Your only twenty-five said Jude.

00:09:23.176 --> 00:09:24.878
That's not old.

00:09:24.938 --> 00:09:27.378
and you can't stop yet.

00:09:27.438 --> 00:09:33.934
He's getting very friendly now, and we can take him to breakfast soon."

00:09:33.994 --> 00:09:42.892
At seven o'clock the club closed, and Jude and Hawker took Johnny back to their hotel.

00:09:42.952 --> 00:09:49.527
Jude picked up the phone and asked for three big breakfasts in the room.

00:09:49.547 --> 00:09:54.033
Hawker took his shoes off.

00:09:54.093 --> 00:09:57.858
That's better, he said.

00:09:57.918 --> 00:10:00.378
He looked at Johnny.

00:10:00.438 --> 00:10:03.890
How often do you go clubbing, Johnny?

00:10:03.950 --> 00:10:07.241
And what do you do in the daytime?

00:10:07.301 --> 00:10:09.122
Not a lot.

00:10:09.182 --> 00:10:11.002
Sleep, usually.

00:10:11.062 --> 00:10:13.733
I go clubbing most nights.

00:10:13.793 --> 00:10:15.644
Where do you live?

00:10:15.704 --> 00:10:17.304
Hawker asked.

00:10:17.364 --> 00:10:20.436
On the streets, said Johnny.

00:10:20.496 --> 00:10:25.834
When I'm rich, I'm going to get a boat and live on that.

00:10:25.894 --> 00:10:29.254
Rich, Jude said.

00:10:29.314 --> 00:10:34.146
Oh yes, we all want to be rich.

00:10:34.206 --> 00:10:40.078
But I am going to be rich, Johnny said.

00:10:40.138 --> 00:10:43.250
I've got a good story.

00:10:43.310 --> 00:10:44.430
See?

00:10:44.490 --> 00:10:46.201
He laughed.

00:10:46.261 --> 00:10:48.974
I'm going to sell it.

00:10:49.034 --> 00:10:57.647
A newspaper wants to give me 100,000 euros for it.

00:10:57.708 --> 00:11:08.009
They gave me 1,000 last month, and I'm going to get the other 99,000 very soon.

00:11:08.069 --> 00:11:11.440
Great, said Jude.

00:11:11.500 --> 00:11:16.081
So, what's the story then, Johnny?

00:11:16.141 --> 00:11:18.300
Have some more coffee.

00:11:18.360 --> 00:11:21.420
and tell us all about it."

00:11:21.480 --> 00:11:26.540
Well, you know the Tyler Drug Company?

00:11:26.600 --> 00:11:28.271
Johnny began.

00:11:28.331 --> 00:11:31.911
They make drugs and medicines.

00:11:31.972 --> 00:11:34.582
Yes, Hawker said.

00:11:34.642 --> 00:11:37.523
It's a very big European company.

00:11:37.583 --> 00:11:41.153
They've got offices in all the big cities.

00:11:41.213 --> 00:11:45.296
Yeah, that's right, Johnny said.

00:11:45.356 --> 00:11:53.724
Well, they're taking young people off the streets and using them for tests.

00:11:53.784 --> 00:11:55.946
Jude laughed.

00:11:56.006 --> 00:12:00.541
Nobody's going to believe that, she said.

00:12:00.600 --> 00:12:06.966
Drug companies use animals, not people for their tests.

00:12:07.026 --> 00:12:11.749
Some new drugs can be very dangerous at first.

00:12:11.809 --> 00:12:16.872
Nobody wants people to die from a new medicine.

00:12:16.932 --> 00:12:21.685
It's true, Johnny said, angrily.

00:12:21.745 --> 00:12:23.966
Think about it.

00:12:24.026 --> 00:12:28.820
All those young, homeless people in London.

00:12:28.880 --> 00:12:34.534
They sleep every night along the Strand and other streets.

00:12:34.594 --> 00:12:37.436
Nobody wants to know them.

00:12:37.496 --> 00:12:40.767
Nobody asks questions about them.

00:12:40.827 --> 00:12:46.116
They've got no home, no family, nothing.

00:12:46.176 --> 00:12:49.337
But they've got legs, Hawker said.

00:12:49.397 --> 00:12:51.458
They can run away.

00:12:51.518 --> 00:12:56.199
You don't understand, said Johnny.

00:12:56.259 --> 00:13:03.161
Listen, I know because I was there.

00:13:03.221 --> 00:13:06.470
I live on the streets, right?

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:14.709
And late one night, along the strand, they came and took me and some other people.

00:13:14.769 --> 00:13:17.560
A boy and two girls.

00:13:17.620 --> 00:13:21.371
They wanted to help us, they said.

00:13:21.431 --> 00:13:27.753
Hot food, nice beds, new clothes, everything.

00:13:27.813 --> 00:13:31.944
They took us to this big house.

00:13:32.004 --> 00:13:33.355
Where?

00:13:33.415 --> 00:13:34.788
said Hawker.

00:13:34.848 --> 00:13:38.684
"'I'm not saying where,' said Johnny.

00:13:38.704 --> 00:13:41.397
"'And what happened?'

00:13:41.456 --> 00:13:42.547
asked Jude.

00:13:42.567 --> 00:13:50.273
"'They gave us food and new clothes and beds to sleep in, all right.

00:13:50.293 --> 00:13:53.935
"'But we couldn't get out of the house.

00:13:53.955 --> 00:13:59.519
"'And men in white coats watched us all the time.

00:13:59.539 --> 00:14:04.073
"'And they put drugs in our food.

00:14:04.133 --> 00:14:06.294
How do you know that?"

00:14:06.354 --> 00:14:08.075
Hawker asked.

00:14:08.135 --> 00:14:10.326
I felt ill.

00:14:10.386 --> 00:14:16.228
My eyes went strange, and I couldn't see very well.

00:14:16.288 --> 00:14:22.329
And one of the girls, she got very ill one night.

00:14:22.390 --> 00:14:28.762
She screamed and screamed, and the men in white coats came.

00:14:28.822 --> 00:14:39.722
I was in the next room, and I listened through the wall This is very strange," one of the men said.

00:14:39.782 --> 00:14:46.157
She had twenty grams of coplast in her dinner tonight.

00:14:46.217 --> 00:14:49.810
Was that too much, do you think?

00:14:49.870 --> 00:14:53.664
I don't know, said a second man.

00:14:53.724 --> 00:14:56.346
We don't want to kill her.

00:14:56.406 --> 00:15:04.892
Let's try twenty grams again tomorrow, on this girl and on one of the boys.

00:15:04.952 --> 00:15:08.173
We can't stop this test now.

00:15:08.233 --> 00:15:12.104
We must get answers quickly."

00:15:12.164 --> 00:15:18.635
After that, they talked more quietly, and I couldn't hear.

00:15:18.695 --> 00:15:31.048
But I didn't eat any more food in that house, and the next night I got into an office downstairs and took some papers.

00:15:31.108 --> 00:15:37.590
Then I broke out of the house and ran away fast.

00:15:37.650 --> 00:15:39.401
What papers?

00:15:39.461 --> 00:15:40.972
said Hawker.

00:15:41.032 --> 00:15:46.916
Papers with Tyler drug companies name on them.

00:15:46.976 --> 00:15:51.118
And where are those papers now?

00:15:51.178 --> 00:15:52.959
asked Jude.

00:15:53.020 --> 00:15:57.522
That's my secret, Johnny said.

00:15:57.582 --> 00:16:07.880
When the newspaper gives me the money, I'm going to tell them but I'm not going to tell you."

00:16:07.940 --> 00:16:16.834
The next day, Jude and Hawker flew back to Brussels and went to Arla's office.

00:16:16.894 --> 00:16:23.286
Arla listened to Johnny Cook's story, but he didn't say anything.

00:16:23.346 --> 00:16:28.558
So, what do we do now, Jude said?

00:16:28.618 --> 00:16:38.288
Do we look for this big house and Arla picked up his telephone, come back in an hour, he said.

00:16:38.348 --> 00:16:41.810
Get a coffee or something.

00:16:41.870 --> 00:16:47.564
An hour and three coffees later, they went back.

00:16:47.624 --> 00:16:50.636
Okay, said Arla.

00:16:50.696 --> 00:16:54.658
You can forget all about this.

00:16:54.718 --> 00:16:59.160
Cook's story isn't true.

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:02.073
Jude stared at him.

00:17:02.133 --> 00:17:04.305
Who told you that?"

00:17:04.365 --> 00:17:05.906
she said.

00:17:05.966 --> 00:17:08.959
I wanted to talk to Johnny Cook again.

00:17:08.979 --> 00:17:10.970
Hawker said.

00:17:11.031 --> 00:17:14.413
You can't, said Arla.

00:17:14.474 --> 00:17:17.106
He's dead.

00:17:17.166 --> 00:17:22.310
Hawker looked at Jude and then back at Arla.

00:17:22.370 --> 00:17:26.804
He was alive yesterday, said Hawker.

00:17:26.863 --> 00:17:31.250
Well, he isn't alive today.

00:17:31.310 --> 00:17:40.668
He came out of a club at three o'clock this morning and fell in the river Thames.

00:17:40.728 --> 00:17:44.950
When they got him out, he was dead.

00:17:45.010 --> 00:17:50.242
But Jude began, forget it, Jude.

00:17:50.302 --> 00:17:54.684
The file is closed.

00:17:54.744 --> 00:17:58.816
And was that the end of it?

00:17:58.876 --> 00:18:00.124
I asked.

00:18:00.184 --> 00:18:04.044
when Jude and Hawker finished telling the story.

00:18:04.104 --> 00:18:06.764
Yes, said Hawker.

00:18:06.824 --> 00:18:10.806
Arla never spoke about it again.

00:18:10.866 --> 00:18:16.658
And did you believe Johnny's story about the drug company?

00:18:16.718 --> 00:18:18.378
I asked.

00:18:18.438 --> 00:18:28.804
Before a company can sell a new medicine to people, said Hawker, there are years and years of tests.

00:18:28.864 --> 00:18:40.634
They do the tests on animals, of course, but they learn much more quickly from tests on people.

00:18:40.694 --> 00:18:50.820
There are lots of drug companies and every company wants to be the first with a new medicine.

00:18:50.880 --> 00:19:03.415
About five years later, Jude said, the Tyler drug company began to sell a new drug called Coplastin.

00:19:03.475 --> 00:19:09.220
It was a medicine to stop some kinds of cancer and it worked.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:11.471
Everybody wanted it.

00:19:11.531 --> 00:19:21.348
The company made a lot of money and so the government got a lot of money from the company in taxes.

00:19:21.408 --> 00:19:35.504
Governments like rich companies and big fat taxes They're not very interested in homeless young people sleeping on the streets.

00:19:35.564 --> 00:19:45.150
So Johnny Cook's story was true, I said, and he didn't fall into the river.

00:19:45.210 --> 00:19:48.422
Somebody pushed him.

00:19:48.481 --> 00:19:53.334
Of course they pushed him, said Jude.

00:19:53.394 --> 00:19:56.466
Dead men can't talk.

00:19:56.526 --> 00:20:06.909
Can they?

00:20:06.969 --> 00:20:23.967
Omega File 451 Loch Ness, Scotland.

00:20:24.027 --> 00:20:31.612
I want you to take the next plane to Scotland, said Arla.

00:20:31.673 --> 00:20:35.846
Then get up to Loch Ness.

00:20:35.906 --> 00:20:38.698
Oh, great, said Hawker.

00:20:38.758 --> 00:20:41.910
Are we looking for the Loch Ness monster?

00:20:41.970 --> 00:20:43.811
Old Nessie?

00:20:43.871 --> 00:20:45.638
Jude laughed.

00:20:45.698 --> 00:20:48.895
Don't laugh, said Arla.

00:20:48.955 --> 00:20:53.068
You are looking for a monster.

00:20:53.128 --> 00:20:56.450
Oh, come on, Arla," Jude said.

00:20:56.510 --> 00:20:59.042
You don't mean that.

00:20:59.102 --> 00:21:06.948
This photo came by email from Edinburgh, said Arla.

00:21:07.008 --> 00:21:08.580
Look.

00:21:08.640 --> 00:21:13.127
He turned to his computer and opened a file.

00:21:13.187 --> 00:21:19.324
It's a night-time photo and not very good.

00:21:19.384 --> 00:21:25.265
Hawker and Jude stared the photo on the computer screen.

00:21:25.325 --> 00:21:35.648
They could see water and something big and grey, half in and half out of the water.

00:21:35.708 --> 00:21:41.450
It's got arms and a head, said Hawker.

00:21:41.510 --> 00:21:44.364
But what is it?

00:21:44.424 --> 00:21:56.264
It kills sheep, cats and dogs," Arla said, and perhaps small children next.

00:21:56.325 --> 00:22:06.490
People in Fort Augustus are screaming at London, and London is screaming at us.

00:22:06.550 --> 00:22:09.862
Go and find it.

00:22:09.922 --> 00:22:14.338
What do we do with it when we find it?

00:22:14.398 --> 00:22:15.502
asked Jude.

00:22:15.522 --> 00:22:18.725
"'Kill it,' said Arla.

00:22:18.745 --> 00:22:23.899
"'Before it kills you.'"

00:22:23.959 --> 00:22:33.017
Hawker and Jude waited for a minute, but Arla turned away and began to read his emails.

00:22:33.037 --> 00:22:37.922
"'Are you telling us everything, Arla?'

00:22:37.982 --> 00:22:39.622
asked Hawker.

00:22:39.683 --> 00:22:42.194
"'Of course!'

00:22:42.254 --> 00:22:45.456
Arla put his hands on the table.

00:22:45.516 --> 00:22:49.950
There were only two fingers on his left hand.

00:22:50.010 --> 00:22:54.254
I always tell you everything.

00:22:54.314 --> 00:22:56.635
You know that.

00:22:56.696 --> 00:22:58.058
Ha!

00:22:58.118 --> 00:23:00.459
said Jude.

00:23:00.519 --> 00:23:11.516
They took a plane to Inverness, then drove along the side of Loch Ness to Fort Augustus.

00:23:11.576 --> 00:23:15.476
It was a grey November day.

00:23:15.536 --> 00:23:21.640
Grey sky, grey water, grey hills.

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:26.002
Hawker looked across the lock.

00:23:26.062 --> 00:23:31.556
It's easy to believe in monsters here, he said.

00:23:31.616 --> 00:23:37.500
Lock Ness is about two hundred metres deep.

00:23:37.560 --> 00:23:44.008
The third deepest lake in Europe Did you know that?

00:23:44.068 --> 00:23:48.462
A hundred monsters could live down there.

00:23:48.522 --> 00:23:52.913
How are we going to find this thing?"

00:23:52.973 --> 00:23:54.824
asked Jude.

00:23:54.884 --> 00:24:00.597
Talked to people in Fort Augustus first, Hawker said.

00:24:00.657 --> 00:24:04.019
Then take it from there.

00:24:04.078 --> 00:24:12.762
They talked to people in their hotel, and to people in the streets in Fort Augustus.

00:24:12.822 --> 00:24:16.942
Everybody had a lot to say.

00:24:17.002 --> 00:24:24.014
It killed Mrs. Fraser's dog, said one woman.

00:24:24.075 --> 00:24:28.996
She has a house down by the water.

00:24:29.056 --> 00:24:34.919
The monster came into her garden one night.

00:24:34.979 --> 00:24:45.721
Her little dog went to look, and the monster killed him Just like that.

00:24:45.782 --> 00:24:53.726
Killed six of my brother's sheep, said a man called Dougal.

00:24:53.786 --> 00:24:58.390
He's very angry about it.

00:24:58.450 --> 00:25:01.362
Can we meet your brother?

00:25:01.422 --> 00:25:02.952
Asked Jude.

00:25:03.012 --> 00:25:06.415
Ask him some questions.

00:25:06.475 --> 00:25:16.854
Dougal's brother, Archie, lived in the Morristan about nine kilometers up the lock.

00:25:16.914 --> 00:25:23.066
He was a big man with black hair and blue eyes.

00:25:23.126 --> 00:25:27.570
He was not very friendly at first.

00:25:27.630 --> 00:25:30.051
Who are you?

00:25:30.111 --> 00:25:31.702
He asked.

00:25:31.762 --> 00:25:35.404
Are you army people?

00:25:35.464 --> 00:25:38.086
No, said Hawker.

00:25:38.146 --> 00:25:40.917
Why do you ask that?

00:25:40.977 --> 00:25:48.100
There's an army laboratory in the hills above the lock.

00:25:48.160 --> 00:25:59.614
Lots of strange people there, and lots of boats on the lock at night coming and going.

00:25:59.674 --> 00:26:04.326
Hmm, interesting, said Jude.

00:26:04.386 --> 00:26:14.938
But tell us about the Loch Ness Monster, and your dead sheep It wasn't Nessie.

00:26:14.998 --> 00:26:20.310
Nessie doesn't kill sheep, Archie said.

00:26:20.370 --> 00:26:26.502
This thing broke their necks.

00:26:26.562 --> 00:26:29.073
Did you see it?

00:26:29.133 --> 00:26:30.643
asked Toker.

00:26:30.703 --> 00:26:38.915
Well, I saw something big, but it moved very fast.

00:26:38.976 --> 00:26:47.176
It was back in the lock in seconds, and it was nearly dark.

00:26:47.236 --> 00:26:50.417
Right, said Hawker.

00:26:50.477 --> 00:27:00.578
Now, we'd like to look at your dead sheep, please, and then we need a boat.

00:27:00.638 --> 00:27:05.549
Where can we get a fast boat, Archie?

00:27:05.610 --> 00:27:09.672
What do you want a boat for?

00:27:09.731 --> 00:27:19.180
We're going to catch this thing," said Jude, and stop it, killing your sheep.

00:27:19.240 --> 00:27:30.819
For the next four days, Hawker and Jude went up and down Loch Ness in Archie Campbell's boat.

00:27:30.880 --> 00:27:35.514
They talked to everybody around the lock.

00:27:35.574 --> 00:27:40.006
When you see this monster, please ring us.

00:27:40.066 --> 00:27:48.016
Anytime, day or night, our mobile phones are always turned on.

00:27:48.076 --> 00:28:05.629
They slept a little in the day and were out most of the night in the boat, with their guns, cameras, mobile phones, a big flashlight, and liters of hot coffee.

00:28:05.689 --> 00:28:13.594
Once, they thought they saw the monster just north of Inver Morriston.

00:28:13.654 --> 00:28:20.688
Another night, a call came from a little place called Foyers.

00:28:20.748 --> 00:28:25.050
They got there at six in the morning.

00:28:25.110 --> 00:28:31.564
It was dark and cold, and everything was very quiet.

00:28:31.624 --> 00:28:37.618
They sat in the boat, looking up and down the lock.

00:28:37.678 --> 00:28:45.931
lock, whispered Hawker, down there by the trees.

00:28:45.991 --> 00:28:53.854
Fifty meters away there were some tall trees by the side of the lock.

00:28:53.914 --> 00:29:01.646
There were some sheep under the trees and something big and dark.

00:29:01.706 --> 00:29:10.598
Suddenly the sheep began to run Start the engine, said Hawker.

00:29:10.658 --> 00:29:13.760
Let's get down there."

00:29:13.820 --> 00:29:24.356
When they got to the trees, they found five sheep with broken necks, but no monster.

00:29:24.416 --> 00:29:31.240
It just kills and goes away again, said Jude.

00:29:31.300 --> 00:29:33.610
Horrible.

00:29:33.670 --> 00:29:42.686
The next night, They were near Erkut Castle when they saw two other boats.

00:29:42.746 --> 00:29:46.208
It was three in the morning.

00:29:46.268 --> 00:29:50.480
Those boats again said Hawker.

00:29:50.540 --> 00:29:56.342
We heard their engines last night and the night before.

00:29:56.402 --> 00:29:58.294
Who are they?

00:29:58.354 --> 00:30:01.184
Let's go and see.

00:30:01.244 --> 00:30:06.044
Quietly, their boat moved nearer.

00:30:06.104 --> 00:30:09.902
There were four men in each boat.

00:30:09.962 --> 00:30:15.606
Men in gray, young men with hard faces.

00:30:15.666 --> 00:30:21.368
They watched Hawker and Jude, and said nothing.

00:30:21.428 --> 00:30:26.540
Hello, said Jude, with a friendly smile.

00:30:26.600 --> 00:30:27.921
Who are you?

00:30:27.941 --> 00:30:33.694
A tall man in the nearest boat answered.

00:30:33.754 --> 00:30:36.346
Army, he said.

00:30:36.406 --> 00:30:38.338
Who are you?

00:30:38.398 --> 00:30:43.960
What are you doing out here at this time of night?

00:30:44.020 --> 00:30:50.904
Where visitors, said Jude, looking for Nessie, of course.

00:30:50.964 --> 00:30:53.734
What are you doing?

00:30:53.794 --> 00:30:59.668
There's no monster in this lock, said the tall man.

00:30:59.728 --> 00:31:04.684
Go back to your hotel and go to bed.

00:31:04.744 --> 00:31:10.069
The two army boats moved away, down the lock.

00:31:10.129 --> 00:31:13.440
Nice, said Hawker.

00:31:13.500 --> 00:31:16.500
Very friendly.

00:31:16.560 --> 00:31:20.401
Allah phoned them every morning.

00:31:20.461 --> 00:31:23.722
Get on with it, he said.

00:31:23.782 --> 00:31:28.403
Before this thing kills someone.

00:31:28.463 --> 00:31:33.354
We can't get near it, Jude told him.

00:31:33.414 --> 00:31:41.632
This lock is 36 kilometers long and two kilometers across.

00:31:41.692 --> 00:31:47.948
There are only two of us, and we're not getting any sleep."

00:31:48.008 --> 00:31:52.560
You can sleep later, said Arla.

00:31:52.620 --> 00:31:56.523
Just catch this thing.

00:31:56.583 --> 00:32:02.448
We met some army people last night, Jude said.

00:32:02.508 --> 00:32:05.236
What are they doing here?

00:32:05.296 --> 00:32:09.145
What do they do at their laboratory?"

00:32:09.206 --> 00:32:11.566
The phone went quiet.

00:32:11.626 --> 00:32:15.808
Then, what laboratory?

00:32:15.868 --> 00:32:21.580
The army laboratory in the hills above Loch Ness.

00:32:21.640 --> 00:32:24.272
The phone went dead.

00:32:24.332 --> 00:32:28.773
Well, well, Jude said to Hawker.

00:32:28.833 --> 00:32:31.224
He doesn't know.

00:32:31.284 --> 00:32:34.632
Or he's not telling.

00:32:34.692 --> 00:32:43.040
The monster came out of the lock and killed sheep nearly every night.

00:32:43.100 --> 00:32:53.914
Everybody around the lock wanted to help Hawker and Jude, and their mobile phones never stopped ringing.

00:32:53.974 --> 00:33:02.960
A lot of people thought the monster was Nessie, but Archie knew it wasn't.

00:33:03.020 --> 00:33:12.478
Nessie never killed anything in fifteen hundred years, he said.

00:33:12.538 --> 00:33:16.010
This is something different.

00:33:16.070 --> 00:33:21.664
And it's going to start killing people soon.

00:33:21.724 --> 00:33:25.826
Look, you need some sheep.

00:33:25.886 --> 00:33:28.828
Sheep, said Hoka.

00:33:28.888 --> 00:33:31.377
Do you mean sleep?

00:33:31.437 --> 00:33:36.346
He was very tired after ten nights on the lock.

00:33:36.406 --> 00:33:38.476
Of course!

00:33:38.536 --> 00:33:39.997
said Jude.

00:33:40.057 --> 00:33:42.308
Clever Archie!

00:33:42.368 --> 00:33:46.009
Can you get us some old sheep then?

00:33:46.069 --> 00:33:49.150
Or perhaps we can use Hawker?

00:33:49.211 --> 00:33:52.832
He's nearly an old sheep by now.

00:33:52.892 --> 00:33:54.872
Oh, shut up!

00:33:54.932 --> 00:33:56.821
said Hawker.

00:33:56.881 --> 00:34:10.370
They found a good place between Inver Morriston and Erkut Castle, with some trees by the water, and took their six old sheep there.

00:34:10.430 --> 00:34:16.217
For three nights they watched, but no monster came.

00:34:16.278 --> 00:34:21.042
The men in grey were out every night, too.

00:34:21.102 --> 00:34:29.117
They were never far away from Hawker and Jude, but never came to speak to them.

00:34:29.178 --> 00:34:38.134
On the fourth night, Hawker and Jude arrived at their sheep place later than usual.

00:34:38.193 --> 00:34:46.396
It was a warm, rainy night, soft Scottish rain that never stops.

00:34:46.457 --> 00:34:52.267
When they turned the engine off, everything was quiet.

00:34:52.327 --> 00:34:56.598
Just the rain whispering on the lock.

00:34:56.658 --> 00:35:05.302
Hawker got out of the boat and stood with the flashlight, watching and listening.

00:35:05.362 --> 00:35:10.664
Jude sat in the boat with her gun in her hand.

00:35:10.724 --> 00:35:14.846
Where are the men in grey?

00:35:14.906 --> 00:35:17.001
whispered Hawker.

00:35:17.061 --> 00:35:25.478
don't know," Jude whispered back, behind us, I think.

00:35:25.538 --> 00:35:30.610
Then everything happened at once.

00:35:30.670 --> 00:35:42.694
There was a sudden noise of boats' engines behind them, and at the same time something moved in the water in front of them.

00:35:42.754 --> 00:35:49.382
Ahead and two long arms came out of the water.

00:35:49.442 --> 00:35:52.386
Light shouted Jude.

00:35:52.446 --> 00:35:53.856
Quick!

00:35:53.917 --> 00:36:09.940
Hawker turned on the flashlight, and at once the monster stood up and ran at Hawker through the water, its long arms going for Hawker's head.

00:36:10.000 --> 00:36:13.136
Get down, Hawker!

00:36:13.196 --> 00:36:15.632
screamed Jude.

00:36:15.692 --> 00:36:31.898
In a second, Hawker was under the water, and then came the sound of Jude's gun, once, twice, and then a third time.

00:36:31.958 --> 00:36:40.438
When the monster stopped moving, Hawker and Jude went to look at it.

00:36:40.498 --> 00:36:51.399
It was a greeny black colour, bigger than a man, and with very long arms and legs.

00:36:51.459 --> 00:36:56.402
It had a small head on a long neck.

00:36:56.462 --> 00:37:01.164
It was a strange, horrible thing.

00:37:01.224 --> 00:37:08.786
A minute later, the men in grey arrived in their two boats.

00:37:08.846 --> 00:37:14.967
They got out and came to look at the dead monster.

00:37:15.027 --> 00:37:22.612
Oh dear, the tall man said, poor old Nessie.

00:37:22.672 --> 00:37:28.487
That, said Hawker, is not Nessie.

00:37:28.548 --> 00:37:31.730
So what is it?

00:37:31.790 --> 00:37:36.994
Visitors, aren't you, said the tall man?

00:37:37.054 --> 00:37:39.535
Where from?

00:37:39.595 --> 00:37:45.888
Hawker and Jude stared at him and said nothing.

00:37:45.948 --> 00:37:56.574
Then Jude took something out of her pocket and held it up in front of the tall man's eyes.

00:37:56.634 --> 00:37:59.316
He looked at it.

00:37:59.376 --> 00:38:04.408
Oh, he said, I see.

00:38:04.468 --> 00:38:07.010
E-D-I.

00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:10.619
Don't see many of those.

00:38:10.679 --> 00:38:12.908
Okay.

00:38:12.968 --> 00:38:16.241
What do you want to know?

00:38:16.301 --> 00:38:21.875
What is that thing?

00:38:21.936 --> 00:38:23.978
said Jude.

00:38:24.038 --> 00:38:28.051
The tall man looked unhappy.

00:38:28.111 --> 00:38:36.848
It is, or it was, one of the army's new fighters.

00:38:36.908 --> 00:38:40.472
It got away from our laboratory.

00:38:40.532 --> 00:38:43.943
and we just couldn't catch it.

00:38:44.003 --> 00:38:52.965
But it was alive, a living thing, said Hawker.

00:38:53.025 --> 00:39:01.107
You can make a lot of living things in a laboratory these days, said the tall man.

00:39:01.167 --> 00:39:06.648
Genetic engineering is getting very clever.

00:39:06.708 --> 00:39:10.986
This fighter can run all night.

00:39:11.046 --> 00:39:15.815
live underwater, see in the dark.

00:39:15.876 --> 00:39:17.906
But it's new.

00:39:17.966 --> 00:39:21.888
We haven't got it right yet.

00:39:21.948 --> 00:39:27.740
And it's programmed to kill anything, is it?

00:39:27.800 --> 00:39:30.231
said Jude.

00:39:30.251 --> 00:39:31.621
No, no!

00:39:31.681 --> 00:39:34.222
The tall man said quickly.

00:39:34.282 --> 00:39:36.794
Not this one.

00:39:36.854 --> 00:39:48.388
This one just kills small animals with four legs, sheep, dogs, cats, things like that.

00:39:48.448 --> 00:39:54.409
Well, said Jude, that is nice to know.

00:39:54.469 --> 00:40:03.822
And where are the other monsters, asked Hawker, for killing men, women, and children?

00:40:03.882 --> 00:40:06.676
Things like that.

00:40:06.736 --> 00:40:09.601
The tall man smiled.

00:40:09.662 --> 00:40:13.936
Can't answer that, I'm afraid.

00:40:13.996 --> 00:40:17.718
Talk to your people in Brussels.

00:40:17.778 --> 00:40:21.411
Well, we must get back.

00:40:21.472 --> 00:40:24.334
Lots to do, you know.

00:40:24.394 --> 00:40:26.986
Thanks for your help.

00:40:27.047 --> 00:40:29.318
Bye.

00:40:29.378 --> 00:40:35.320
The men in grey put their dead monster in one of the boats.

00:40:35.380 --> 00:40:42.844
and went away up the lock into the dark and the rain.

00:40:42.904 --> 00:40:47.618
And what did Arla say about it all?

00:40:47.678 --> 00:40:49.340
I asked.

00:40:49.400 --> 00:40:53.582
He was so angry, Hawker said.

00:40:53.643 --> 00:40:56.415
He went crazy.

00:40:56.475 --> 00:41:00.888
He didn't know about the monsters, you see.

00:41:00.948 --> 00:41:03.270
All the laboratory.

00:41:03.330 --> 00:41:08.894
The army didn't tell anyone in Brussels.

00:41:08.954 --> 00:41:16.487
And Arla liked to know everyone's secrets, said Jude.

00:41:16.548 --> 00:41:22.490
Did the army make any more monsters, I asked?

00:41:22.550 --> 00:41:27.072
Not in Scotland, said Hawker.

00:41:27.132 --> 00:41:32.212
The British army closed their laboratory after that.

00:41:32.272 --> 00:41:38.939
The Americans and the French made some monsters years later.

00:41:38.999 --> 00:41:46.790
They were smaller, like big cats, but with eight legs.

00:41:46.850 --> 00:41:50.271
Where are they now, I said?

00:41:50.331 --> 00:41:53.552
You don't hear anything about them?

00:41:53.612 --> 00:41:57.782
Of course not, said Jude.

00:41:57.842 --> 00:42:03.282
People don't want to hear about monsters.

00:42:03.342 --> 00:42:19.600
Therein and Tarktica, or in a place deep under the ground, said Hawker, nice and secret, just waiting for the next war.

00:42:19.660 --> 00:42:29.796
And so there isn't a Loch Ness Monster, and never was one, I said.

00:42:29.856 --> 00:42:38.542
Nessie, said Jude, She looked me in the eyes, and did not smile.

00:42:38.602 --> 00:42:42.874
Of course there's a lock-ness monster.

00:42:42.934 --> 00:42:55.690
She's a blue-gray colour, has a small head, a very long neck, and is about fifteen metres long.

00:42:55.750 --> 00:43:27.057
Go and look at all the photos of her, on the internet, Omega file 522 Galapagos, Ecuador.

00:43:27.117 --> 00:43:32.530
Got your son hats, said Arla.

00:43:32.591 --> 00:43:34.112
Why?

00:43:34.172 --> 00:43:35.733
asked Jude.

00:43:35.793 --> 00:43:38.304
Where are we going now?

00:43:38.364 --> 00:43:42.858
South America, Arla said.

00:43:42.918 --> 00:43:46.390
Big place, said Jude.

00:43:46.450 --> 00:43:48.604
How about Chile?

00:43:48.664 --> 00:43:50.747
I like Chile.

00:43:50.807 --> 00:43:54.209
No, it's Ecuador.

00:43:54.269 --> 00:44:03.574
You're going to the Galapagos Islands, a thousand kilometers out in the Pacific Ocean.

00:44:03.634 --> 00:44:07.228
Oh, right, Hawker said.

00:44:07.288 --> 00:44:10.149
Are you going to tell us why?

00:44:10.169 --> 00:44:14.072
Hala looked unhappy.

00:44:14.132 --> 00:44:19.032
There's something strange going on.

00:44:19.092 --> 00:44:26.661
EDI is getting emails every day from Nagalapagos.

00:44:26.721 --> 00:44:36.124
They're all about Isabella Island, and they all say things like this.

00:44:36.184 --> 00:44:41.036
He gave Hawker and Jude a piece of paper.

00:44:41.096 --> 00:44:50.843
Important news, important news, A new time is coming for our planet.

00:44:50.903 --> 00:44:58.886
The first visitors are now on Isabella Island Galapagos.

00:44:58.946 --> 00:45:01.276
Don't fight them.

00:45:01.336 --> 00:45:03.947
Don't be afraid of them.

00:45:04.007 --> 00:45:06.428
Be friendly.

00:45:06.488 --> 00:45:10.668
Tell your government now.

00:45:10.728 --> 00:45:16.250
Orca and Jude looked at Arla and then laughed.

00:45:16.310 --> 00:45:23.134
There are a lot of crazy people out there on the internet, said Jude.

00:45:23.194 --> 00:45:25.927
You don't believe this one?

00:45:25.987 --> 00:45:27.468
Do you?

00:45:27.529 --> 00:45:30.260
Perhaps it's crazy.

00:45:30.321 --> 00:45:34.704
And perhaps it's not, said Allah.

00:45:34.764 --> 00:45:41.928
But when we email back with questions, they don't answer.

00:45:41.988 --> 00:45:51.572
The Americans are watching the island by satellite, but they don't want to tell us why.

00:45:51.632 --> 00:45:56.874
There are two Australian ships going there.

00:45:56.934 --> 00:46:06.810
The Mexicans are getting very excited, and the Ecuadorians are saying nothing.

00:46:06.870 --> 00:46:11.104
Something is happening on Isabella.

00:46:11.164 --> 00:46:13.274
What is it?

00:46:13.335 --> 00:46:17.005
We want to know.

00:46:17.066 --> 00:46:23.307
From Brussels to the Galapagos is a long way.

00:46:23.367 --> 00:46:37.880
Hawker and Jude took a plane to Cuba, a second plane to Ecuador, then a third plane out to Baltra Island in the Galapagos.

00:46:37.940 --> 00:46:44.328
When they got out of the plane a wall of hot air hit them.

00:46:44.388 --> 00:46:47.480
Oh, said Hawker.

00:46:47.540 --> 00:46:50.712
He put on his sun hat quickly.

00:46:50.772 --> 00:46:58.158
They went across to Santa Cruz Island and down to Puerto Iora.

00:46:58.218 --> 00:47:08.564
There they found a boat, the sea lion, to take them to Isabella, about 90 kilometers away.

00:47:08.625 --> 00:47:15.890
At first The boatman, Gonzalo, did not want to take them.

00:47:15.950 --> 00:47:20.924
My boat can take ten people, he said.

00:47:20.984 --> 00:47:23.636
It's a very good boat.

00:47:23.696 --> 00:47:28.659
But very expensive for only two people.

00:47:28.720 --> 00:47:31.181
Jude smiled at him.

00:47:31.242 --> 00:47:33.212
Not for two.

00:47:33.272 --> 00:47:35.354
Rich people?

00:47:35.414 --> 00:47:37.966
Rich, said Hawker.

00:47:38.026 --> 00:47:41.478
It's not our money, ow!

00:47:41.538 --> 00:47:45.820
Jude hit him hard on the arm.

00:47:45.880 --> 00:47:55.498
Where on holiday, she told Gonzalo, we want to see the giant tortoises on Isabella.

00:47:55.558 --> 00:47:57.600
She looked at Hawker.

00:47:57.660 --> 00:47:59.902
Don't we?

00:47:59.962 --> 00:48:05.246
Yes, that's right, said Hawker quickly.

00:48:05.306 --> 00:48:10.790
We're very interested in the giant tortoises.

00:48:10.850 --> 00:48:22.386
on the way to Isabella Island, Jude read a book about the Galapagos, and Hawker watched the sea.

00:48:22.446 --> 00:48:44.574
Isabella is a very young island, Jude told him, and it has, listened to this, six volcanoes, one erupted only two years ago Oh, that's great," said Hawker.

00:48:44.634 --> 00:48:54.462
Crazy emails, strange visitors in the middle of the Pacific, and now erupting volcanoes.

00:48:54.522 --> 00:48:57.374
Thank you, Arla.

00:48:57.434 --> 00:49:07.290
Not many people lived on Isabella, and Puerto Villamil was usually a sleepy place.

00:49:07.350 --> 00:49:15.101
But when the sea lion arrived, There were about fifty people down by the sea.

00:49:15.162 --> 00:49:18.822
There were two small boats.

00:49:18.882 --> 00:49:33.108
And on them, Hawker and Jude could see chairs and tables, beds, boxes and bags and a bicycle.

00:49:33.168 --> 00:49:39.033
Gonzalo called out in Spanish to the people on the boats.

00:49:39.093 --> 00:49:42.285
Then, turned to Hawker and Jude.

00:49:42.305 --> 00:49:47.248
"'Lots of people are leaving Isabella,' he said.

00:49:47.268 --> 00:49:49.589
"'They are afraid.'"

00:49:49.609 --> 00:49:52.441
"'Afraid of what?'

00:49:52.501 --> 00:49:53.572
asked Jude.

00:49:53.592 --> 00:49:56.664
"'Go and talk to them Hawker.

00:49:56.724 --> 00:50:00.026
Your Spanish is better than mine.'"

00:50:00.086 --> 00:50:04.411
Hawker came back half an hour later.

00:50:04.472 --> 00:50:08.986
"'You're not going to believe this,' he told Jude.

00:50:09.006 --> 00:50:15.428
"'The people here say there's a spaceship on Isabella.

00:50:15.488 --> 00:50:26.372
It came down ten days ago, right down inside Volcano Aceido, and it's still there.

00:50:26.392 --> 00:50:29.613
"'How do they know that?'

00:50:29.673 --> 00:50:30.653
said Jude.

00:50:30.673 --> 00:50:37.560
"'There's an Australian Dr. Jim Miller up on Alcedo.

00:50:37.620 --> 00:50:42.462
He works here studying giant tortoises.

00:50:42.522 --> 00:50:51.166
He saw the spaceship and now he's waiting for the visitors to come out.

00:50:51.226 --> 00:51:07.764
So the visitors in those emails are extraterrestrials, ETs, little green men from another planet Oh, dear, said Jude.

00:51:07.824 --> 00:51:11.244
Can we go home now, Hawker?

00:51:11.304 --> 00:51:13.326
Hawker laughed.

00:51:13.386 --> 00:51:16.366
No, we can't.

00:51:16.426 --> 00:51:20.728
We climb volcano acedo, he said.

00:51:20.788 --> 00:51:23.280
Talk to Dr. Miller.

00:51:23.340 --> 00:51:26.590
Say hello to the E.T.'s.

00:51:26.650 --> 00:51:30.252
Oh, dear, Jude said again.

00:51:30.312 --> 00:51:33.122
I was afraid of that.

00:51:33.182 --> 00:51:39.554
Gonzalo took them in the sea lion up to Shipton Cove.

00:51:39.614 --> 00:51:49.362
There, very early the next morning, Hawker and Jude began their climb up the volcano.

00:51:49.422 --> 00:52:02.417
There is a path, Gonzalo told them, but it is five hours to the top and hard climbing and very, very hot.

00:52:02.477 --> 00:52:11.694
You must carry water, two liters for one person, for one day.

00:52:11.754 --> 00:52:18.016
You must sleep at the top and come down tomorrow.

00:52:18.076 --> 00:52:23.028
But not when the sun is high in the sky.

00:52:23.088 --> 00:52:27.810
And be careful, please.

00:52:27.870 --> 00:52:31.671
Careful of the space-visitors, you mean?

00:52:31.731 --> 00:52:33.425
Said Jude.

00:52:33.485 --> 00:52:45.762
I don't know about space ships," smiled Gonzalo, but volcano Ascedo is always a little excited.

00:52:45.822 --> 00:52:50.544
She is always doing something new.

00:52:50.604 --> 00:52:54.975
It was a very hard climb.

00:52:55.035 --> 00:52:59.956
After two hours they stopped under some trees.

00:53:00.016 --> 00:53:06.188
They drank some water and looked out over the blue sea.

00:53:06.248 --> 00:53:13.032
The black volcanic rocks under their feet were hot from the sun.

00:53:13.092 --> 00:53:18.684
It's so beautiful here, said Jude.

00:53:18.744 --> 00:53:23.788
Hmm, yes and no, said Hawker.

00:53:23.848 --> 00:53:33.572
Then, hey, Jude, look, that animal, over there by that rock.

00:53:33.632 --> 00:53:36.434
What is it?

00:53:36.494 --> 00:53:38.656
Oh, wow!"

00:53:38.716 --> 00:53:40.556
whispered Jude.

00:53:40.616 --> 00:53:42.928
It's an iguana.

00:53:42.988 --> 00:53:46.110
A galapagos iguana.

00:53:46.170 --> 00:53:49.614
Isn't he wonderful?

00:53:49.674 --> 00:53:57.970
The iguana stared at them with its hot, orange eyes and did not move.

00:53:58.030 --> 00:54:05.658
Its body was about a meter long and an orange, yellowy colour.

00:54:05.718 --> 00:54:14.676
It looks about a thousand years old, said Hawker, a very strange animal.

00:54:14.736 --> 00:54:21.181
Everything about this island is strange, said Jude.

00:54:21.242 --> 00:54:28.666
They climbed and climbed, and the sun got hotter and hotter.

00:54:28.726 --> 00:54:46.045
After three more hours, they came to the top, and looked down into the great crater of Alcedo, two hundred meters deep and seven kilometers across.

00:54:46.106 --> 00:55:05.115
To the north and the south, they could see more volcanoes, and across the sea to the west, the island of Fernandina, but they could not see Dr. Miller or his camp.

00:55:05.175 --> 00:55:10.866
We need to go round the crater to the south, said Hawker.

00:55:10.926 --> 00:55:15.948
It's another two hours walk, the villagers said.

00:55:16.008 --> 00:55:24.140
It was hard walking over the black lava rock and once Hawker nearly fell.

00:55:24.200 --> 00:55:26.640
Jude caught his arm.

00:55:26.700 --> 00:55:30.277
Don't break a leg here, she said.

00:55:30.337 --> 00:55:33.234
I don't want to carry you back down to the boat."

00:55:33.254 --> 00:55:35.695
"'Why not?"

00:55:35.755 --> 00:55:37.315
said Hawker.

00:55:37.376 --> 00:55:39.456
"'I carried you home once."

00:55:39.476 --> 00:55:46.288
"'We weren't on top of a volcano then," said Jude.

00:55:46.348 --> 00:55:54.902
At last they saw Dr. Miller's camp, and ten minutes later they arrived.

00:55:54.962 --> 00:56:01.536
Dr. Miller was short, very brown, and angry.

00:56:01.596 --> 00:56:04.757
"'Go away,' he shouted.

00:56:04.777 --> 00:56:08.380
"'You're Americans, aren't you?'

00:56:08.400 --> 00:56:12.823
"'No, we aren't,' said Hawker.

00:56:12.843 --> 00:56:15.324
"'We're European.

00:56:15.384 --> 00:56:18.026
How do you do, Dr. Miller?

00:56:18.086 --> 00:56:20.948
"'What are you doing here?'

00:56:21.009 --> 00:56:22.350
he said angrily.

00:56:22.370 --> 00:56:29.052
"'We'd like to talk to you,' said Jude quietly.

00:56:29.112 --> 00:56:33.262
about the spaceship down in the crater.

00:56:33.322 --> 00:56:36.234
Why are you so angry?

00:56:36.294 --> 00:56:42.566
Because nobody listens to me, said Dr. Miller.

00:56:42.626 --> 00:56:45.767
Nobody believes me.

00:56:45.827 --> 00:56:50.789
The Americans say, oh, crazy man.

00:56:50.849 --> 00:56:56.081
The Australian government says, get some sleep.

00:56:56.141 --> 00:56:58.664
What can I do?

00:56:58.724 --> 00:57:07.738
Something very important is happening on this planet and nobody is listening.

00:57:07.798 --> 00:57:14.600
Well, we're here now and we're listening, Jude said.

00:57:14.660 --> 00:57:17.621
Dr Miller looked at them.

00:57:17.682 --> 00:57:20.802
Who do you work for?

00:57:20.862 --> 00:57:23.464
Europe, said Hawker.

00:57:23.524 --> 00:57:27.820
Europe is very interested in this spaceship.

00:57:27.880 --> 00:57:31.576
Please, tell us about it.

00:57:31.636 --> 00:57:38.350
Ah, the e-mails did get through then, said Dr. Miller.

00:57:38.410 --> 00:57:44.142
Who did the e-mails come from, asked Hawker?

00:57:44.202 --> 00:57:49.024
Ecuadorian friends, said Dr. Miller.

00:57:49.084 --> 00:57:51.776
Over on Santa Cruz.

00:57:51.836 --> 00:57:55.638
Look, I've got some beer here.

00:57:55.698 --> 00:57:57.766
You want one?

00:57:57.826 --> 00:58:06.470
They sat on the black lava rocks under the hot sun and drank hot beer.

00:58:06.530 --> 00:58:16.398
Below them, clouds of smoke and steam moved this way and that way across the crater.

00:58:16.458 --> 00:58:24.408
And was there under those clouds a spaceship from another planet?

00:58:24.468 --> 00:58:32.106
Sometimes I think I can see it down there," said Jim Miller.

00:58:32.167 --> 00:58:35.219
But mostly I can't.

00:58:35.279 --> 00:58:43.374
It's a great white thing, and long legs came out of it when it came down.

00:58:43.435 --> 00:58:45.826
But why here, Jim?

00:58:45.886 --> 00:58:47.158
said Jude.

00:58:47.218 --> 00:58:50.489
Why, into a volcano?

00:58:50.550 --> 00:58:52.661
Who knows?

00:58:52.722 --> 00:58:54.041
said Jim.

00:58:54.101 --> 00:58:57.471
Perhaps they like hot places.

00:58:57.531 --> 00:59:02.362
Perhaps they need something from the hot lava.

00:59:02.422 --> 00:59:06.403
And why are you angry with the Americans, Jim?"

00:59:06.463 --> 00:59:07.924
Hawker asked.

00:59:07.984 --> 00:59:16.336
I know their beer's no good, but they watched this spaceship on their satellite.

00:59:16.396 --> 00:59:18.316
I know they did.

00:59:18.377 --> 00:59:24.208
They know it's here, but they don't want the world to know.

00:59:24.268 --> 00:59:31.880
They don't want people like you and me to meet any extraterrestrial visitors.

00:59:31.940 --> 00:59:37.522
Oh no, they want it all to be a big secret.

00:59:37.582 --> 00:59:41.574
Then they can be top dog.

00:59:41.634 --> 00:59:45.625
Just then, there was a sudden noise.

00:59:45.685 --> 00:59:49.216
A boom, deep below the ground.

00:59:49.276 --> 00:59:50.537
What?

00:59:50.597 --> 00:59:52.757
What was that, Jim?

00:59:52.818 --> 00:59:54.566
asked Jude.

00:59:54.626 --> 01:00:00.306
Oh, how sadow does that all the time, said Jim.

01:00:00.366 --> 01:00:09.671
Then hot water comes up and steam, dust, sometimes a little lava, but not much.

01:00:09.731 --> 01:00:14.373
That's why there are always clouds in the crater.

01:00:14.433 --> 01:00:18.114
You can never see anything down there.

01:00:18.174 --> 01:00:22.146
Can we climb down into the crater?

01:00:22.206 --> 01:00:23.658
asked Hawker.

01:00:23.718 --> 01:00:25.850
"'Are you crazy?

01:00:25.910 --> 01:00:30.292
It's dangerous down there,' Jim said.

01:00:30.352 --> 01:00:42.976
All evening, Hawker and Jude stared down into the crater, but they could see nothing through the clouds of steam and dust.

01:00:43.036 --> 01:00:57.509
Just before the sun went down, Hawker saw something near the top of the crater and shouted to Jude but it was only two of the giant tortoises.

01:00:57.569 --> 01:01:05.852
They came slowly past the camp and went away down the other side of the volcano.

01:01:05.912 --> 01:01:17.156
Later, four more came past, going the same way, moving slowly and quietly over the black rocks.

01:01:17.216 --> 01:01:22.500
They're very strange animals, said Jude.

01:01:22.560 --> 01:01:26.934
Hawker and Jude did not sleep much.

01:01:26.994 --> 01:01:37.492
The rocks were hard, and below them they heard again and again the deep boom of the volcano.

01:01:37.552 --> 01:01:42.546
Late in the night they turned their radio on.

01:01:42.606 --> 01:01:50.270
It was very noisy, but through the noise they could hear a voice from Santa Cruz.

01:01:50.330 --> 01:01:59.236
Hawker listened hard They're talking about volcano alcedo," he said.

01:01:59.296 --> 01:02:05.248
They think it's going to erupt in the next 24 hours.

01:02:05.308 --> 01:02:07.598
Jude sat up.

01:02:07.658 --> 01:02:09.369
Oh, no!

01:02:09.429 --> 01:02:12.990
We're seven hours away from the boat.

01:02:13.050 --> 01:02:15.030
Let's get moving.

01:02:15.091 --> 01:02:17.722
Go and call Jim.

01:02:17.782 --> 01:02:23.335
But Jim Miller did not believe Santa Cruz radio.

01:02:23.396 --> 01:02:27.270
It's the Americans again," he said.

01:02:27.330 --> 01:02:30.824
They want us all to go away.

01:02:30.884 --> 01:02:34.496
Please come with us, Jim, said Jude.

01:02:34.556 --> 01:02:39.110
Please, you can come back in a day or two.

01:02:39.170 --> 01:02:42.722
You too go, said Jim.

01:02:42.783 --> 01:02:49.458
But I'm staying right here and watching that spaceship.

01:02:49.518 --> 01:02:52.741
It was a hard climb down.

01:02:52.801 --> 01:02:59.046
When they got to the sea, they saw Gonzalo with the little boat.

01:02:59.107 --> 01:03:00.777
Hurry!

01:03:00.838 --> 01:03:02.188
He shouted.

01:03:02.248 --> 01:03:09.734
Did you hear, on the radio, as say those going to erupt?

01:03:09.794 --> 01:03:16.070
Quickly, they went out to the sea lion and climbed up onto the boat.

01:03:16.130 --> 01:03:17.430
Go!

01:03:17.490 --> 01:03:18.491
Go!

01:03:18.551 --> 01:03:19.802
Go!

01:03:19.862 --> 01:03:22.442
Gonzalo shouted to his men.

01:03:22.502 --> 01:03:28.791
and before long, the sea lion was a kilometer out at sea.

01:03:28.851 --> 01:03:34.722
Two hours later, volcano Alcedo erupted.

01:03:34.783 --> 01:03:44.064
There was a sudden great bang, and then clouds of dust flew up into the sky.

01:03:44.124 --> 01:03:52.144
Red-hot lava came out of the volcano's sides and ran down to the sea.

01:03:52.205 --> 01:04:07.852
The noise did not stop, and with every bang rocks flew hundreds of metres up into the sky, then fell slowly back down to the ground.

01:04:07.912 --> 01:04:16.768
For hours the night sky was filled with great flowers of red and orange light.

01:04:16.828 --> 01:04:23.705
It was a beautiful and a terrifying thing to watch.

01:04:23.765 --> 01:04:27.618
What happened to Dr. Miller?"

01:04:27.678 --> 01:04:29.319
I asked.

01:04:29.379 --> 01:04:36.300
Poor Jim went to the great spaceship in the sky, Jude said.

01:04:36.360 --> 01:04:43.392
Five hundred meters of red-hot lava fell on top of him.

01:04:43.452 --> 01:04:48.033
And was there a spaceship in the volcano?

01:04:48.093 --> 01:04:50.853
No, said Jude.

01:04:50.914 --> 01:04:54.154
Yes, said Hawker.

01:04:54.214 --> 01:04:58.406
He looked at Jude, and they laughed.

01:04:58.466 --> 01:05:01.548
Then Jude looked at me.

01:05:01.609 --> 01:05:04.700
What do you want to believe?

01:05:04.760 --> 01:05:06.292
She asked.

01:05:06.352 --> 01:05:11.114
They weren't very clever extraterrestrials were they?

01:05:11.174 --> 01:05:19.445
Sitting there in their spaceship in an erupting volcano Orca smiled.

01:05:19.505 --> 01:05:27.168
Ah, but perhaps the spaceship left, just before the volcano erupted.

01:05:27.228 --> 01:05:40.466
Gonzalo and I saw something in the clouds of dust, a white light moving very fast, faster than the dust.

01:05:40.526 --> 01:05:43.826
It went up very high.

01:05:43.886 --> 01:05:48.607
"'Well, I didn't see anything,' said Jude.

01:05:48.627 --> 01:05:55.222
"'And that's because there wasn't anything in that volcano.'

01:05:55.283 --> 01:05:58.915
Hawker looked up into the blue, Greek sky.

01:05:58.935 --> 01:06:03.078
"'How do we know?'

01:06:03.138 --> 01:06:04.419
he said slowly.

01:06:04.439 --> 01:06:13.438
"'One day, someone or something is going to visit us from out there.

01:06:13.498 --> 01:06:22.028
Perhaps that was the first visit all those years ago in the Galapagos.

01:06:22.088 --> 01:06:23.672
Who knows?

